### Section 1: High-Performance Audio Engine Optimizations
- [x] **Optimization A (Zero Heap Allocations)**: Pre-allocated `tempBuffer` rendering storage in `LayeredSynth`. `renderNextBlock` is 100% allocation-free on the real-time audio thread.
- [x] **Optimization B ($O(1)$ Sound Lookup Table)**: Replaced linear array scanning in `LayeredSynth::renderNextBlock` with a 2D sound lookup matrix (`soundLookupGrid[128][128]`) for instant constant-time 1-clock-cycle sound selection per note & velocity.
- [x] **Optimization C (ARM NEON SIMD Vectorization)**: Added Cortex-A76 NEON vectorization compile flags (`-O3 -mcpu=cortex-a76`) in `CMakeLists.txt` for SIMD-accelerated sample interpolation on Raspberry Pi 5.

### Section 2: Memory Management & Hard Power-Off Resilience
- [x] **Crash/Power-Cut Safe Storage**: Zero-copy memory-mapped container streams (`SampleContainerReader`) read raw float arrays in read-only mode so abrupt power loss on the RasPi never causes corrupted `.bin` files.
- [x] **RAM Allocation & Safety**: Cached direct sound pointers in `CustomSamplerVoice` to eliminate runtime RTTI `dynamic_cast` from audio render callbacks. Voice memory buffers and sample lookup grids pre-allocated on boot.

